{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205885-new-gm-question","id":1205885,"title":"New GM Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T20:17:36-07:00","id":1205885,"title":"New GM Question","content":"(Just to clarify, new to running Changeling, not a new GM)<br /> <br /> I just wondered how conducive Changeling the Dreaming (20th Ann.) was for a single player and one GM? Also, when I googled this question, I got a lot of hits on what to look out for when starting a Changeling Campaign, but all them pertained to previous editions. Anything in the new edition I should look out for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:25:06-07:00","id":1205892,"title":"","content":"...that depends. What are some specifics on this 1 player chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:30:45-07:00","id":1205896,"title":"","content":"I don't see any particular issues with having one ST and one player, and it avoids the question of how this motley gets along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:33:47-07:00","id":1205898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205885-new-gm-question?p=1205892#post1205892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that depends. What are some specifics on this 1 player chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, I haven't come up with any. <br /> <br /> To back up a little, I am familiar with the setting concepts of Changeling but I've never actually played or run it. Since the game always intrigued me, I participated in the Deluxe Kickstarter. I received my physical copy yesterday and shared the unboxing with my wife\u2014who really does know very little about it. She was struck how beautiful and cool it looked, so I started kicking around the idea of preparing a 1-player chronicle. Something fun to do together. But some games seem really dependent on multiple players while others do not, so I was checking the feasibility before I got her hopes up or got myself heavily invested.<br /> <br /> Sorry I don't have any specifics beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:51:20-07:00","id":1205902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205885-new-gm-question?p=1205898#post1205898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I haven't come up with any. <br /> <br /> To back up a little, I am familiar with the setting concepts of Changeling but I've never actually played or run it. Since the game always intrigued me, I participated in the Deluxe Kickstarter. I received my physical copy yesterday and shared the unboxing with my wife\u2014who really does know very little about it. She was struck how beautiful and cool it looked, so I started kicking around the idea of preparing a 1-player chronicle. Something fun to do together. But some games seem really dependent on multiple players while others do not, so I was checking the feasibility before I got her hopes up or got myself heavily invested.<br /> <br /> Sorry I don't have any specifics beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be fine. There are no specifics on running a 1 player chronicle, but there's very little actually about how to make the game run for a group either. And C20 neither makes it harder or easier to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:59:57-07:00","id":1205903,"title":"","content":"You should be fine, I hear a lot of games played between spouses. Remember this frees you up to have the story concentrate on one player, and making a motley of NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:04:34-07:00","id":1205905,"title":"","content":"Ok then to that end...yeah, a 1 player chronicle should be fine.<br /> <br /> Either just have a story of a changeling trying to get by and getting Glamour each and every day should do fine. A (relatively) low-power game of the changeling just exploring the weird and strange happenings around their town. Might be hard to do a politics-heavy-freehold game since you'd have to account for a bunch of characters, but if you and the wife are up for it, go right ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:41:33-07:00","id":1205934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205885-new-gm-question?p=1205905#post1205905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then to that end...yeah, a 1 player chronicle should be fine.<br /> <br /> Either just have a story of a changeling trying to get by and getting Glamour each and every day should do fine. A (relatively) low-power game of the changeling just exploring the weird and strange happenings around their town. Might be hard to do a politics-heavy-freehold game since you'd have to account for a bunch of characters, but if you and the wife are up for it, go right ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly unless you have a larp or similar type game you are going to have to run most of the politics as the St anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:26:55-07:00","id":1205948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205885-new-gm-question?p=1205903#post1205903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be fine, I hear a lot of games played between spouses. Remember this frees you up to have the story concentrate on one player, and making a motley of NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have the 1st rule: Never mix your women and the RPGs. It usualy gets messy.<br /> <br /> But the 1 player one ST game is fine with CtD, but sometimes tireing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}